body:
@rdlh Thanks, and sorry for our own slow turnaround. That settles the first question: your 0.27.1 arm ran with async scheduling ON, so the 12/4800 is consistent with the async-gated path that #51571/#53919 describe. It doesn't show an async-independent mechanism, and your nightly 0/4800 fits that fix lineage.

Yes, please add the block-boundary variant if it's cheap. It exercises a different path: a prefix-cache hit on a block whose recurrent state was written during decode, over positions that may include rejected MTP drafts. That is what #57128 targets (`MambaManager.find_longest_cache_hit` accepts `drop_eagle_block` but doesn't act on it), and it would not be covered by the async fix. A run on a current release (0.29.x/0.30.0) with `--no-async-scheduling` would separate the two cleanly. A gist of the script would help too.

(Written with AI assistance, reviewed by me.)
